CommitDate: Thu Jul 2 00:37:39 2026 -0500

    REL-RC-N: prose-plan harvest + force-submit ladder hole
    
    Attempt 6 lane a6 iter 1 (conv_86142c62): model emitted its plan as
    prose 9 times, ignored every reminder, and the force-submit marker
    NEVER fired (the valve only armed on a different trigger path) —
    actionless pause, 3 resume re-loops, NO_REPLAN_AFTER_REVISION.
    
    Two-layer fix: (1) generalized event-derived force marker so the
    narrowing ladder actually arms on prose-planning segments; (2) after
    the ladder is exhausted and the model still emits prose, the host
    HARVESTS the plan from the model's own prose message (numbered/bulleted
    steps, cap 8; fallback = pending user instruction as one step — the
    REL-RC-F precedent), synthesizes a FRESH PlanEvent (new id, correct
    next revision), routes it through the SAME autonomous approval gate,
    and records the harvest in a loud system-reminder. Real submit_plan
    always preempts. All segment-scoped signals are replayable.
    
    Blank-planning spins now recover instead of halting at the bound
    (test_replan_pending_valve updated to the improved behavior).
    
    Fable review rejected two worker changes: removing asyncio.to_thread
    from the C18 done-condition probe (would block the event loop up to 5s
    per probe to fix a sandbox-only test hang) and the companion test-scope
    reduction — both reverted; test passes unmodified in the real env.
    
    Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.5); investigation, reverts, and gating by
    Fable. Gates: basedpyright 0, full packages+harness green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0148WNDs6Jw33bq3eTt8qgCm

