Implemented REL-RC-P. The loop now derives the repeated actionless-pause signal from events, emits a durable synthetic-finish marker, and on eligible resume routes a synthetic `finish(summary=...)` through the existing finish pipeline and gates.

Key changes:
- [signals.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/loop/signals.py:160): replayable pause-pair signal, productive reset, one-attempt-per-pause marker, latest prose summary.
- [finish.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/loop/finish.py:2750): synthetic finish helper emits the loud reminder, then calls `normalize_finish_step` + `handle_finish_path`.
- [engine.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/loop/engine.py:950): pre-model resume hook, skipped in planning mode.
- [test_synthetic_finish_actionless.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/tests/test_synthetic_finish_actionless.py:136): success, dictated-content refusal, planning/no-productive guards, replay rebuild coverage.

